	(text "Simulation copy of power_latch.kicad_sch (hand-synced, not linked): Inspect > Simulator, Run, then add signals,\ne.g. V(3V3_EN), V(/K), V(/VK), V(VBUS), V(PWR_OFF), V(/BTN). Models: AO3400A/AO3401A as VDMOS (Vth 1.05 / -0.9 V),\nMMBT3904 = 2N3904 Gummel-Poon, 1N4148. SW101 is a voltage-controlled switch driven by V4.\nDefault run: 0.1 s USB plugged -> ON. 1.0 s PWR_OFF -> OFF (still plugged, stays off). 1.5 s button -> ON.\n2.2 s PWR_OFF -> OFF. 2.6 s unplug, 3.0 s replug -> ON. 4-14 s button held: forced OFF after 6-9 s (R108/C104 -> Q104),\nstays off after release with USB still plugged. 15 s short press -> ON. V5 stands in for the LDO (only R107 uses +3V3).\nmethod=gear: the default trapezoidal integration rings at the switching edges (fake +-10 mA spikes on I(V1)).\nSource currents follow SPICE sign convention: a source that delivers power shows negative I and P; plot -I(V1).\nV1 inserts a 3.7 V cell at t=0 (C101 must keep the latch off). Dead cell: set V1 to pwl=\"0 0 0.4 0 0.41 3.6\"\n(VSYS appears 300 ms after the plug-in) to check the kick still latches; other cell voltages: change 3.7.\nWorst-case Vth: change vto in the Sim.Params of Q101-Q105 (0.65-1.45 V AO3400A, -0.6..-1.3 V AO3401A). Keep ksubthres=0.02:\nthe VDMOS default (0.1) leaks far more below threshold than real FETs and falsely re-latches in the low-Vth corner."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "09193406-88e0-4f1c-b9c4-5de5fbf9e933")
	)
	(text ".tran 1m 16\n.options method=gear"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 174 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1b7b8028-aa85-4f9a-b53d-4bbc428fe66a")
	)
	(text "Soft power latch, all JLC Basic parts. Q101/Q102 hold 3V3_EN on without firmware; SW101 sets it through R105/D101.\nOff: firmware drives PWR_OFF high (Q103), or the button is held 6-9 s (R108/C104 charge until Q104 conducts).\nFirmware: PWR_BTN is low while the button is pressed. Before driving PWR_OFF, WAIT FOR THE BUTTON TO BE RELEASED,\nor the held button re-latches the rail when 3V3 collapses. Keep PWR_OFF high until power is gone.\nC101 keeps Q101 off on VSYS steps (cell inserted, USB plugged). Verified in ngspice over 48 corners (Vth, hFE, 3.0-4.2 V, leakage).\nUSB plug-in turns it on: the VBUS edge through C105 sets K via D103/R110 (~0.5 s pulse, R109 bleeds C105), so the\nfirmware can raise the charge current. Only the edge: switched off while plugged in, it stays off. Simulated in ngspice:\nlatches with VSYS 3.0-4.2 V, VBUS ramps up to 100 ms, and a dead cell when VSYS comes up to 350 ms after VBUS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 71.12 127 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "faccdf49-b228-4ba5-9f95-27d12c27cd5e")
	)
